From 6ee8c8d8cf5dbfd4ac3cbe1f6cf5998e6137491e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:18:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-74: the Properties panel's top like WPF's: the
 Name box, Properties / Events (0.74.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "我需要你把此外掛軟體改得跟WPF 操作模式一樣" / "一小部分一小部分搜尋、
小部分修改". Part 2, from Microsoft's "Create UIs with Visual Studio XAML
Designer > Properties window":
- "Change the name of the currently selected element in the Name box": the
  Name box is at the top (the type beside it); a new name + Enter renames (one
  commit: Enter, its key release, change). The Name row of 外觀與版面 and the
  pencil button are gone (F2 on the design surface still renames).
- "To see the list of events for a control, click the Events button, which
  appears as a lightning bolt symbol": 〔屬性〕〔⚡ 事件〕 -- ONE list at a time;
  the events list = the 事件表 + the page's JS events, everything else in the
  properties list; the choice is remembered. The search box searches the list
  shown.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 158, smoke 160, panels, real VS Code 147): panels
(the properties list by default, the lightning bolt = the events list only and
back; the Name box: spbSave, a new name + Enter posts rename once; a handler
name found in the events list).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
